  "rewritten_text": "Megan Gray is a historian in her 30s living in a small house in the Midwest. A first-generation Irish American, she grew up reading the local archives with her mother and spent her weekends volunteering at the DuPage County Historical Society. After graduating with honors in History from the University of Chicago, she took a research assistant position at the Smithsonian, where she focuses on early 20th-century urban migration. Megan writes her articles in English and contributes regularly to the regional journal Midwest History Review.\n\nOutside of work, Megan shares a small house with her older brother, Michael, and keeps close ties to her parents, Linda and Robert, who encouraged her passion for the past. She describes herself as an atheist and aligns with liberal political ideas, often participating in community forums about historic preservation. In her free time, she enjoys documenting oral histories from longtime residents of her region, hoping to turn her fieldwork into a book that will highlight the everyday lives of ordinary people."
 },
