  "rewritten_text": "Richard Donnelly, in his early 40s, has spent most of his adult life among the stacks of a public library, where he now serves as senior librarian. A native of York County, he grew up speaking English and identifies as Irish. After earning a BA in History from the University of Maine, he completed his MLS at Simmons College, and his early career saw him cataloguing collections at the Portland Regional Library and later at an academic library before returning home in the early 2010s. His keen eye for organization and a love of local history helped him launch the town’s digital archives project, a partnership that involved working with the state historic preservation office and a nonprofit group.\n\nOff the clock, Richard lives locally with his wife, Maya, and their two teenage children, Nora and Declan. A practicing Catholic, he attends Mass on Sundays and volunteers as a literacy tutor for adult learners. Politically, he describes himself as moderate and often contributes to town council discussions about public funding for cultural programs. In his spare time he enjoys sailing on nearby waters, collecting first-edition novels, and organizing the annual summer reading festival that brings together families from across York County."
 },
