  "rewritten_text": "Somchai Vongpradit is a senior editor in his late sixties who splits his time between his home at 42 Maple Ct in the New York metropolitan area and the bustling newsrooms of New York City. After earning a BA in English from the University of California, Los Angeles, and an MA in Publishing from a university, he began his career as a copy editor at The New York Times before moving on to a long stint at a major publishing house, where he helped shape dozens of nonfiction titles. He now leads the editorial team at a small publishing house, guiding new voices and overseeing the final polish of manuscripts that range from memoirs to investigative journalism.\n\nOutside the office, Somchai is a devoted Buddhist and an active member of his local temple, where he volunteers to teach writing workshops to youth. A lifelong Republican, he frequently writes op-eds on media ethics and free speech. He and his wife, Pim, have raised three children—two daughters and a son—who live throughout the United States, and they enjoy regular visits from six grandchildren who love hearing stories about his early days in the industry."
 },
