  "rewritten_text": "Farid Rahimi is an experienced carpenter who lives in a coastal community in the southeastern United States. An Iranian American, he grew up hearing stories of his grandparents’ craft in Tehran and turned that heritage into a lifelong love of woodwork. After earning an associate’s degree in construction technology from the University of Florida, Farid began his career with a construction firm, later moving to a custom woodworking firm where he helped design and restore dozens of homes along the Gulf. He now runs his own carpentry shop, specializing in handmade furniture and historic renovation projects.\n\nFarid is a Muslim and a progressive who votes for candidates who support workers’ rights and environmental stewardship. He shares his home with his wife, Parisa, and their two adult children, Sara and Arman, who occasionally join him in the workshop on weekends. When he isn’t shaping oak or pine, Farid enjoys fishing in the Everglades and volunteering at the local community garden, where he mentors younger craftsmen and promotes sustainable building practices."
 },
